{"$schema":"https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"artifacts":[{"contents":{"text":"<scxml xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml\" version=\"1.0\" initial=\"a\">\n  <state id=\"a\"><transition target=\"b\"/></state>\n  <state id=\"b\"><transition target=\"c\"/></state>\n  <state id=\"c\"><transition target=\"a\"/></state>\n</scxml>\n"},"location":{"uri":"tests/ui/lint004-eventless-cycle-three-states.scx"},"mimeType":"application/scxml+xml"}],"columnKind":"utf16CodeUnits","properties":{"diagnosticCounts":{"errors":0,"notes":0,"total":1,"warnings":1},"producer":{"kind":"validator"}},"results":[{"level":"warning","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/lint004-eventless-cycle-three-states.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":38,"endLine":2,"startColumn":37,"startLine":2}}}],"message":{"markdown":"unconditional eventless transition cycle: a -> b -> c -> a\n\n**Note:** eventless, conditionless transitions are taken immediately in the same macrostep; a cycle of them never reaches a stable configuration (a warning: SCXML 1.0 Appendix D says a macrostep that does not terminate \"is currently allowed\", so the document is conforming and compiles, and a host bounds the run)\n\n**Help:** add an event or condition to one transition, or remove a target so the macrostep can reach a stable configuration\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §3.13 Selecting and Executing Transitions","text":"unconditional eventless transition cycle: a -> b -> c -> a"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":111,"start":110},"category":"lint"},"relatedLocations":[{"id":1,"message":{"text":"`a` declared here"},"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/lint004-eventless-cycle-three-states.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":15,"endLine":2,"startColumn":14,"startLine":2}}},{"id":2,"message":{"text":"then `b` enters `c`"},"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/lint004-eventless-cycle-three-states.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":38,"endLine":3,"startColumn":37,"startLine":3}}},{"id":3,"message":{"text":"then `c` enters `a`, closing the cycle"},"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/lint004-eventless-cycle-three-states.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":38,"endLine":4,"startColumn":37,"startLine":4}}}],"ruleId":"LINT004"}],"tool":{"driver":{"informationUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/","name":"scxml-validator","rules":[{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"eventless, conditionless transitions are taken immediately in the same macrostep; a cycle of them never reaches a stable configuration (a warning: SCXML 1.0 Appendix D says a macrostep that does not terminate \"is currently allowed\", so the document is conforming and compiles, and a host bounds the run)"},"help":{"text":"How to fix: add an `event` or `cond` to one edge of the cycle, or remove one target.\n\nSpecification: SCXML 1.0 §3.13 Selecting and Executing Transitions\n\nRun `scx --explain LINT004` for examples."},"helpUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/#SelectingTransitions","id":"LINT004","name":"LINT004","properties":{"category":"lint"},"shortDescription":{"text":"unconditional eventless transitions form a cycle"}}],"semanticVersion":"0.2.0"}}}],"version":"2.1.0"}